        "subject": "LU-21211 ldlm: optimize client lock enqueue handling",
        "message": "LU-21211 ldlm: optimize client lock enqueue handling\n\nThe server LDLM enqueue path does not need to process locks that\nare a different type from the namespace, running useless lock-type\nprocessing for a request that did not fit that namespace.\n\n - ldlm_handle_enqueue() fetched a reply field from a request that\n   packed no reply message\n - A request named a lock type the namespace did not serve (an MDT\n   serves IBITS, FLOCK and quota PLAIN locks; an OST serves EXTENT;\n   the MGS serves PLAIN).  Record the namespace type at creation\n   and skip a mismatched or unsupported type, so per-type processing\n   never runs on a lock its resource does not need to process.\n - ldlm_inodebits_add_lock() and ldlm_inodebits_unlink_lock() walked\n   the inodebits queues through a server lock that has no inodebits\n   node; skip it in both (only the add_lock granted branch did so\n   before).\n - ldlm_flock_blocking_ast() assumed a cancellation and unlinked the\n   lock from the deadlock list; return early for any other flag.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I79d4b9ec6a0c4972e0da4235a60475ac1b3ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70338\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Zhuravlev <azhuravlev@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
